WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.515
The next night.

2
00:00:01.615 --> 00:00:03.691
Your friend Sam's on passing duty.

3
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.544
Chalk's out of goal, chasing.

4
00:00:05.762 --> 00:00:07.004
Your back's to the goal.

5
00:00:07.134 --> 00:00:08.075
You face Sam.

6
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.445
The pass comes.

7
00:00:09.587 --> 00:00:10.416
Stiff foot.

8
00:00:10.883 --> 00:00:11.726
It bounces away.

9
00:00:12.143 --> 00:00:12.892
You look up.

10
00:00:15.141 --> 00:00:16.572
Chalk's already there.

11
00:00:16.946 --> 00:00:17.706
Ball gone.

12
00:00:18.094 --> 00:00:19.774
You had the ball for two seconds.

13
00:00:19.994 --> 00:00:21.036
It felt like nothing.

14
00:00:21.557 --> 00:00:22.763
Where did the time go?

15
00:00:23.992 --> 00:00:25.983
This ring is your time.

16
00:00:26.096 --> 00:00:30.774
It counts the seconds until Chalk reaches
the ball, if he keeps coming at a jog.

17
00:00:30.814 --> 00:00:33.398
Sprinting shrinks the
numbers, not the fixes.

18
00:00:33.835 --> 00:00:37.230
When the pass arrived:
just over half a second.

19
00:00:37.596 --> 00:00:38.977
One heartbeat.

20
00:00:39.685 --> 00:00:40.707
Remember this ring.

21
00:00:41.802 --> 00:00:44.074
Football isn't only a game of speed.

22
00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:45.550
It's a game of time.

23
00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:47.516
The best players look slow.

24
00:00:48.073 --> 00:00:50.637
They bought time before anyone noticed.

25
00:00:51.061 --> 00:00:52.112
Three ways to buy it.

26
00:00:52.581 --> 00:00:53.145
Look.

27
00:00:53.549 --> 00:00:54.236
Touch.

28
00:00:54.438 --> 00:00:55.042
Shape.

29
00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:58.052
By lights out: four times the time.

30
00:01:00.775 --> 00:01:02.364
Way one: look.

31
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.477
Before the ball comes,
look over your shoulder.

32
00:01:05.547 --> 00:01:07.211
You know this one: a scan.

33
00:01:07.584 --> 00:01:09.359
A snapshot, not a stare.

34
00:01:09.622 --> 00:01:10.806
Click, and back.

35
00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.418
Your eyes barely stop.

36
00:01:12.825 --> 00:01:14.885
One question: where's Chalk?

37
00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.310
Pros do it right up to the touch.

38
00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.077
Why not look after it arrives?

39
00:01:20.429 --> 00:01:23.572
Noticing something new:
about a third of a second.

40
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.856
Choosing what to do: about half a second.

41
00:01:27.124 --> 00:01:28.983
That's two of Chalk's steps.

42
00:01:29.164 --> 00:01:32.062
Like checking for cars
after stepping off the kerb.

43
00:01:32.205 --> 00:01:33.035
Check first.

44
00:01:33.208 --> 00:01:34.143
Then move.

45
00:01:35.104 --> 00:01:36.133
So look early.

46
00:01:36.512 --> 00:01:38.593
Ball leaves Sam's foot: look.

47
00:01:39.035 --> 00:01:40.690
Halfway: look again.

48
00:01:41.143 --> 00:01:42.434
Then eyes on the ball.

49
00:01:42.867 --> 00:01:43.657
Where's Chalk?

50
00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.030
Where's the space?

51
00:01:45.517 --> 00:01:46.961
They build a map in your head.

52
00:01:47.031 --> 00:01:48.135
You know what's behind you.

53
00:01:49.016 --> 00:01:51.764
Elite youth players: one
look before the ball?

54
00:01:51.896 --> 00:01:54.442
Three times the odds of a good next move.

55
00:01:54.926 --> 00:01:56.029
Did the look cause it?

56
00:01:56.401 --> 00:01:57.581
Nobody's proved that.

57
00:01:57.904 --> 00:01:59.049
It went with it.

58
00:01:59.373 --> 00:02:02.606
Small, but free, dozens of times a game.

59
00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:06.334
Know early, move early, even one step.

60
00:02:06.825 --> 00:02:07.985
The ring's there before the ball.

61
00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:11.945
Classic mistake: eyes glued to the ball.

62
00:02:12.103 --> 00:02:15.154
Fix: ball leaves the foot, head goes.

63
00:02:15.425 --> 00:02:16.759
Two coloured cones behind you.

64
00:02:16.972 --> 00:02:18.663
Sam passes and calls one.

65
00:02:18.774 --> 00:02:22.405
Look back, find it, shout left or
right before the ball's halfway.

66
00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:23.606
Late call?

67
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.628
Doesn't count.

68
00:02:24.885 --> 00:02:26.080
Slow passes first.

69
00:02:26.902 --> 00:02:28.979
Way two: touch.

70
00:02:29.086 --> 00:02:32.211
Your first touch decides your next second.

71
00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:35.500
The ball doesn't bounce off
just because your boot's hard.

72
00:02:35.691 --> 00:02:39.557
Mostly it's the speed gap:
fast ball, still foot.

73
00:02:40.114 --> 00:02:41.739
Big gap, big bounce.

74
00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.356
Catch an egg with a stiff hand: splat.

75
00:02:44.638 --> 00:02:46.304
Move with it: safe.

76
00:02:47.037 --> 00:02:51.102
Stiff, still foot: it leaves
at maybe a third of its speed.

77
00:02:51.414 --> 00:02:53.874
Now move your foot back with it.

78
00:02:54.103 --> 00:02:55.297
The gap shrinks.

79
00:02:55.337 --> 00:02:56.884
The bounce dies.

80
00:02:57.154 --> 00:02:58.016
That's a cushion.

81
00:02:58.455 --> 00:03:01.367
Contact: about a hundredth of a second.

82
00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:02.914
Far shorter than a blink.

83
00:03:03.104 --> 00:03:05.538
So be soft before it lands.

84
00:03:06.447 --> 00:03:08.653
Step one: kill the bounce.

85
00:03:08.881 --> 00:03:11.532
With Chalk coming, it buys nothing alone.

86
00:03:11.881 --> 00:03:15.137
One touch into space, away
from Chalk, buys metres.

87
00:03:15.355 --> 00:03:18.736
At Chalk's jog, every two
metres is about half a second.

88
00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.331
Pros: touch, touch, gone.

89
00:03:21.678 --> 00:03:23.566
Your first touch is the steering wheel.

90
00:03:24.471 --> 00:03:27.918
Classic mistake: killing
it dead under your feet.

91
00:03:28.197 --> 00:03:31.424
Fix: soft foot, aimed where you're going.

92
00:03:31.682 --> 00:03:32.982
Wall drill, alone.

93
00:03:33.348 --> 00:03:34.315
Cushion the return.

94
00:03:34.936 --> 00:03:37.404
Then one touch out of a
box, away from a cone.

95
00:03:37.444 --> 00:03:38.482
Swap feet.

96
00:03:38.522 --> 00:03:39.623
Start soft.

97
00:03:39.663 --> 00:03:42.859
The car park has suffered enough.

98
00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.404
Way three: shape.

99
00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.760
How you stand.

100
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.467
Arms out wide.

101
00:03:48.507 --> 00:03:50.746
You see everything between your hands.

102
00:03:50.847 --> 00:03:52.245
A bit more than a half circle.

103
00:03:52.285 --> 00:03:55.930
Sharp only in a thumbnail-sized
spot at arm's length.

104
00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:56.814
The rest: blur.

105
00:03:56.987 --> 00:03:59.737
It catches movement, not whose shirt.

106
00:04:00.705 --> 00:04:02.227
Face Sam straight on.

107
00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:03.236
Goal behind you.

108
00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.524
Chalk lives there.

109
00:04:04.639 --> 00:04:06.354
To play forward, you turn.

110
00:04:06.742 --> 00:04:09.879
A full turn costs over half a second.

111
00:04:10.311 --> 00:04:12.677
Timed on youth players
running and turning, no ball.

112
00:04:13.178 --> 00:04:15.635
That's your whole ring
from the first pass.

113
00:04:16.563 --> 00:04:18.436
Now stand side-on.

114
00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:19.498
The half-turn.

115
00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.955
Old cue, new reason.

116
00:04:22.087 --> 00:04:25.373
Sam in the corner of one
eye, the goal in the other.

117
00:04:25.888 --> 00:04:27.741
The corner of your eye catches movement.

118
00:04:28.062 --> 00:04:29.344
The look tells you who.

119
00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.340
Every look is now a small turn.

120
00:04:33.398 --> 00:04:35.959
Take it on your back foot,
the one further from Sam.

121
00:04:36.243 --> 00:04:37.540
Toes where you're going.

122
00:04:37.996 --> 00:04:40.629
It rolls across you,
train through a station.

123
00:04:40.873 --> 00:04:44.074
Half-turned, back foot:
no turn to pay for.

124
00:04:44.114 --> 00:04:46.638
You play forward while
the ring's still big.

125
00:04:47.563 --> 00:04:51.300
Classic mistake: facing the
passer with room to turn.

126
00:04:51.582 --> 00:04:54.234
Fix: side-on, before the pass.

127
00:04:54.617 --> 00:04:55.654
Two gates behind you.

128
00:04:55.837 --> 00:04:57.902
Sam calls a gate, then passes.

129
00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.369
Open to that gate.

130
00:04:59.631 --> 00:05:02.176
Back foot, one touch
through it, pass back.

131
00:05:02.525 --> 00:05:03.780
Easy passes first.

132
00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:08.432
One more way: steal time.

133
00:05:08.472 --> 00:05:11.404
Shoulders one way, ball the other.

134
00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:16.686
One test, adult players: a fake cost
the defender about half a second.

135
00:05:17.056 --> 00:05:19.338
Two of Chalk's steps, stolen.

136
00:05:20.082 --> 00:05:21.420
But that's for another night.

137
00:05:22.465 --> 00:05:24.096
The first pass again.

138
00:05:24.612 --> 00:05:26.905
It leaves Sam's foot: look.

139
00:05:27.027 --> 00:05:29.975
Chalk, about ten metres out, jogging in.

140
00:05:30.627 --> 00:05:31.297
Don't wait.

141
00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:33.908
Go to the ball, opening side-on.

142
00:05:34.561 --> 00:05:36.767
Halfway: look again.

143
00:05:37.342 --> 00:05:38.133
Still far.

144
00:05:39.036 --> 00:05:39.703
Back foot.

145
00:05:40.101 --> 00:05:41.856
It rolls across you.

146
00:05:42.266 --> 00:05:44.718
Soft touch, into space.

147
00:05:45.131 --> 00:05:46.257
Away from Chalk.

148
00:05:46.692 --> 00:05:47.437
Read the ring.

149
00:05:47.859 --> 00:05:49.738
Almost two and a half seconds.

150
00:05:51.644 --> 00:05:52.529
Chalk arrives.

151
00:05:53.645 --> 00:05:54.443
To nothing.

152
00:05:55.081 --> 00:05:56.089
Same legs.

153
00:05:56.129 --> 00:05:57.101
Same speed.

154
00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.933
Four times the time.

155
00:05:59.209 --> 00:06:03.134
You looked earlier, moved
earlier, and met the ball side-on.

156
00:06:03.227 --> 00:06:05.960
Then one touch where Chalk wasn't.

157
00:06:06.493 --> 00:06:08.370
That's why the best players look slow.

158
00:06:09.631 --> 00:06:11.198
Where did the time go?

159
00:06:11.426 --> 00:06:12.285
Nowhere.

160
00:06:12.421 --> 00:06:14.685
You bought it before anyone noticed.

161
00:06:14.843 --> 00:06:15.913
Lights out.

162
00:06:16.264 --> 00:06:18.798
Next pass that rolls at
you: take a snapshot.
